index 4479b53..4aa29c3 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,17 +1,26 @@
-# The DevTools Times
+# smallpt Render Lab
 
-This project is a sample news application built with Astro, designed to serve as a testing ground for new features in Chrome DevTools.
+Kevin Beason’s MIT-licensed [smallpt](https://www.kevinbeason.com/smallpt/), compiled from C++ to WebAssembly and displayed on the home page. The Astro build prerenders the page to `dist/client/index.html`.
 
+## Build
+
+Requires Node.js, pnpm, and Emscripten (`em++` on PATH).
 
 ```sh
-pnpm install && pnpm run start
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
+pnpm build
 ```
 
-The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
+`pnpm build:wasm` rebuilds just `public/smallpt/renderer.js` and `renderer.wasm`. Generated Wasm assets are checked in so the renderer is available without a local compiler. The complete build recompiles them before building Astro.
+
+## Renderer
+
+- `native/smallpt-original.cpp`: unchanged upstream source.
+- `native/smallpt.cpp`: original radiance algorithm and scene, adapted to export initialization, sphere colors, and RGBA row rendering.
+- `public/smallpt/worker.js`: loads the Emscripten ES module in a dedicated worker and transfers row buffers to the UI. No rendering server or cross-origin isolation is required.
+- `src/scripts/lab.ts`: canvas updates, render/stop, resolution and samples, randomized sphere tints, reset, and PNG export.
+- `public/smallpt/reference.png`: upstream smallpt reference image, displayed as a background while the first client-side render arrives. It is replaced by actual WebAssembly output row by row and never used for image export.
 
-## Tech Stack
+The page automatically renders on load. Randomize colors changes both foreground spheres’ reflectance while preserving their original mirror and glass materials. Increasing samples reduces noise and increases rendering time. Stop terminates the current worker; starting another render or randomizing also replaces any in-progress worker.
 
-- **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
-- **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
-- **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
-- **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+The original copyright and MIT license are in `public/smallpt/LICENSE.txt`.
